    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί-στῐχος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with two rows,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριθαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Placit.</u>
					5.10.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>of two verses,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίγραμμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.369
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Cyrill.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίστιχον, τό,</span>
			<i>distich,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.329
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <i>'a couple of lines',</i> of a brief letter, <i><span class="en">
				<u>FGiss.</u>
				20.23
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>doubly woven,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαφόρια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMasp.</u>
					6ii80
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>.</div>
